ee navy because  earth in particular is under constant  threat the line about drummer deciding  to make an uneasy alliance is tied to  what we saw in that mini episode she's  talking to someone we just hear a voice  there's no face no indication of their  affiliation but we know that they need  to refuel and rearm their ship and their  options are limited one thing you can  pick up from the first episode is that  even though the free navy may not be  able to feed all their people they are  making progress in going out and  eliminating the other factions that had  gone against marco so the crew of the  tynan is in a tough spot and they're  looking to put michio somewhere safe out  of harm's way after the mistakes she  made that cost them the dewalt and while  we're talking about them let's get into  this anka wallah scene we first heard  the word anka walla in episode 9 of  season 5. this is how oxana referred to  drummer to crawl when they were talking  about keeping the secret about naomi  being alive the direct translation would  be something like anchor person so you  could think of it as a loved one or a  soulmate and initially i interpreted  this as her putting drummer above the  other members of the polyamorous family  but the expanse writers responded on  twitter that she could refer to any of  them that way you see the words one ship  in the opening and in voice over naomi  introduces the belter creed the doctrine  of one ship so drummer is a combination  of different characters including one  that shares the name with her crewmate  here michio paw we get an explanation of  this doctrine in michio's chapters in  the books it boils down to a belief that  there was only one ship and it had  countless parts as a single body had  countless cells she describes it in  relation to the ships that are under her  and how her little fleet is only a part  of the free navy a vast organism that  passed information between its cells  with tight beam and radio that consumed  food and fuel that worked its own slow  destiny among the planets like a massive  fish in the greater sea of the sky she  talks about her extended crew the others  who served under her came and went  respected that she was captain that her  orders were fair and that she didn't  show any overt favoritism to her spouses  but there was the understanding always  that the core of the ship was her family  and no threat to it would be tolerated  the idea of separating family from crew  was an inner planet's thing one example  of the unconscious prejudice that made  earthers and martians treat life aboard  ships is somehow different from real  life for them the rules changed when the  airlock closed even if they didn't know  themselves well enough to see it for  belters there was no division  so it's a belter-centric way of viewing  things from the perspective of people  who live in space the ship is home it's  not something that you use to get from  point a to point b your family your crew  those are all part of a bigger organism  and everyone has an important role in  working together for its survival so in  the clip we see the reaction to the  bounty being raised when they see the  announcement about that as mentioned  before we do see that drummer has made  contact with someone and they're on  route to resupply they've already  explained to michio that she'll be  dropped off when they do that and she  comes in and tells joseph that she  looked inside drummer's hand terminal  and realized that all of her videos were  things that she saved from naomi this in  and of itself isn't a big revelation to  us we know that oxana brought this up  and more importantly the fact that  marco's wanting her to kill the ross and  nantes so it couldn't save naomi is  exactly why she went against the free  navy drummer didn't do that to save  holden considering that she has strong  feelings for naomi her feelings about  her boyfriend are complicated what  stands out here is that she deletes them  all at the end her family suffered as a  result of her decision her husband serge  paid the ultimate price and while  discovering the videos made michio  question her dedication to the family  her deleting them is an indication that  she regrets the way that things played  out what a great character and i gotta  say it's nice to see michio get a hug  here because that was kind of a rough  ordeal she went through in episode one  so it was an interesting look into  drummer's family on the tynan and we'll  have to wait and see how that becomes  important later they are gonna be doing  one of these with every episode i'm not  sure if they're all gonna be like  extended scenes or if there'll be some  other stuff added in but it's a nice  addition and i look forward to seeing  how they go for the teasers they're both  short one was basically a twitter post  and one was more a traditional teaser  and they're both based on the same thing  and kind of go together so i'll just be  looking at it as one big thing and boy  do i love me some action sequences with  bobby and power armor okay even though  it's gonna sound a little ridiculous  there are some things about these  teasers that i can't confirm because of  the do not reveal lists that amazon  sends out when they give you screeners  you can pretty much put together what's  happening here right you don't need me  to spell it out for you the rossi has  tracked down a ship bobby is wearing  said power armor and the other ship is  making a break for it holden is in the  pilot chair doing his best to keep them  close which at one point that looks like  it has amos pinned to the floor under  thrust everyone's in suits and we can  see that clarissa is preparing an emp  device that bobby will be carrying later  the airlock door in the cargo bay is  open and we hear bobby tell holden to  get her as close as she can she then  jumps out with that emp in hand in a  great looking shot as the ships are  flying side by side and is able to land  safely and after she secures herself she  calls for naomi to follow on the rossi  we see naomi start and then she kind of  freezes up and then we hear holden ask  if she's alright and the teaser ends  there we did see naomi jump out of a  couple of ships in season 5. once  without an air bottle and once with no  suit at all neither of those were  pleasant experiences but it's still kind  of hard to imagine that the crew  wouldn't be able to count on their  resident belter in a situation like this  and as i said wow bobby's leap is just  so weirdly satisfying to behold this is  something that is pulled directly from  the books although the setup is a little  different and there's one major change  that jumps out here so this looks like a  great addition and even in these short  compressed for twitter clips the visual  effects look amazing and i'm gonna have  to wait until the full episode comes out  before i can talk anymore about this the  last thing from the episode description  was that philip is wrestling with his  guilt we saw that start in the last  episode and it was a safe guess that  that would continue he's still a young  man and there's a lot of different  things going on here all of which will  be exasperated by the idea that he shot  somebody on ceres someone who was his  friend so that has an extra weight to it  but also this isn't the wild west you  can't just go around murdering people in  broad daylight on top of that he played  a major part in mass murder he's  starting to see that what his father  says and what his father delivers aren't  exactly the same things and if you think  back to episode one each time he echoed  those ideals that they needed to take  care of the people on series because  that was their people that was their  capital he was quickly brushed aside and  it's implicit that he doesn't understand  how things really work but then also  rosenfeld's there she has his father's  attention and he's not getting this  direct education to help him understand  any of that which i mean is a good thing  objectively but that's not how a young  man who defines himself in relation to  his father would see it so i think  that's probably all there is to say ever  since the first teaser came out i've had  a lot of questions about why they  decided to add the laconia part and i  did make a whole video about why i  thought that made sense so you should  check that out but here i'll just say  that i think it is essential to the  story they're telling in this season  plus it's a great little story so enjoy  it for that reason and just hang in  there because i don't think you'll be  disappointed so let me know in the  comments what you think about the season  so far what you think about these  teasers about the x-ray episode and what  you're hoping to see in the next one  please like this video if you enjoyed it  please subscribe to my channel if you  haven't already and thanks for watching  i'll talk to you soon  you
 

